  "img": "systems/draw-steel/assets/classes/conduit.png",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You are a <strong>rigger</strong> - you fight through a fielded fleet of machines. Your power flows from <strong>Uptime</strong>: the live, humming link between you and every drone under your command, fed by the fleet you keep online. The corp records call you a <em>freelance drone-tech</em>; the street calls you a <strong>Wrench</strong>, the rigger in the walls.</p><p>Your engine is <strong>Uptime</strong>: at the start of each of your turns, gain Uptime for each drone currently fielded under your command (up to a cap). Deploying a <strong>new</strong> drone banks deploy momentum (+2); the first time each round one of your drones lands an effect, bank a link echo (+1). You spend Uptime on heroic abilities and on deploying/sustaining drones. Unspent Uptime is lost at the end of the encounter, and any drones still fielded power down.</p><h3>Signatures &amp; Subclass</h3><p>Three signatures cost no Uptime: <strong>Deploy &amp; Command</strong> (field and command your fleet), <strong>Rigged Fire</strong> (the drone's mounted attack, a Cognition Power Roll - your only personal damage), and <strong>Field Repair</strong> (restore Integrity to drones, vehicles, chrome, and gear). At Tier 5 you choose a subclass - Drone (Swarm-Master), among others - that colors your fleet and grants an identity feature.</p><h3>Advancement (internal Level 1-5 = player-facing Tier 5-1)</h3><p>At <strong>Tier 5</strong> you choose your subclass, gain all three signatures, and pick an opening heroic. Every Tier after, you gain a new heroic ability and your Uptime cap rises. The ladder caps at <strong>Tier 1</strong>.</p>",
      "director": ""
    },
